12306	{"artifactId":"LLD-1716f77ba9ba017b-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-1716f77ba9ba017b-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-05T08:46:29.047Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers every bullet of the ISSUE's fix intent: record the author, route each review to the other party for documents and code, make the gate reject a same-party review with the existing override, rewrite steering/guides/tool descriptions, and keep work with no recorded author approvable.","evidence":"docs/standalone/two-sets-eyes-review-rule-only-E202610041716f77b/ISSUE.md lines 27-33 list five fix-intent bullets. Each maps to the design: 3.1 (party fields), 3.2+3.3 (routing, both tools), 2.5 (gate, override kept), 3.4 (steering, tool descriptions, guides follow the steering source), and the rule 'an unknown author or an unknown reviewer never withholds approval by itself'. The root-cause sites the ISSUE cites exist as described: src/mcp/review-step/phases/findings.ts:32 and verdicts.ts:34 stamp REVIEW_MODEL = 'client'; src/workflow/gates.ts:578 only refuses a blocking review. The design goes further than the ISSUE by requiring a review to exist for DEF/HLD/LLD/BUILD; that is backed by stakeholder citations c5/c6, and an unreviewed legacy artifact stays approvable through a review (unknown author routes to the daemon) or an override. [files: docs/standalone/two-sets-eyes-review-rule-only-E202610041716f77b/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/mcp/review-step/phases/findings.ts, src/mcp/review-step/phases/verdicts.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"For a stream request with no handler the daemon answers with a plain `{ id, error: 'unknown method: ...' }` line with no `stream` field and leaves the socket open, and the existing MCP stream helper ignores any line whose `stream` is not progress/delta/done/error.","evidence":"src/daemon/server.ts:186-203: handleStreamMessage falls back to a standard handler, else `this.send(socket, { id: request.id, error: `unknown method: ${request.method}` }); return;` with no socket end. src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts:149-163 acts only on the four stream kinds and falls through at `// Unknown stream kind — ignore (forward-compatible).` Note: runWorkflowStream has no timer of its own, so against an old daemon it would hang until the socket closes; the timeout the design mentions can only come from the new tool-side wait limit, which the design does add. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts]","action":"None. Keep the wait-limit timer in the new helpers, since the existing helper has none.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"In insrc_code_review_step's start phase, 'only a freshness check that is UNAVAILABLE returns an error and starts no review, as today'; the phase has four outcomes today.","evidence":"src/mcp/code-review-step/handler.ts has two more error exits that start no review. Lines 303-306: `const g = await deps.fetchGrounding(...); if (!g.ok) { return errorResult('grounding-unavailable', ...) }`. Lines 355-358 in beginDiffOnlyReview: `if (err instanceof DiffUnavailableError) { return errorResult('diff-unavailable', ...) }`. The four outcomes the design lists are otherwise accurate (confirm_wait at 291-298, decline at 229-232, wait timeout at 272-279, empty symbols at 312-313), and the stated daemon gap is real: src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts:93 calls runCodeReview with only runId, modelLabel, signal and onProgress. The omission matters because the design moves diff grounding to the daemon, so it must say where each of these two errors now surfaces, and T17 tests neither. [files: src/mcp/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts]","action":"Amend 3.3 to list the two extra error outcomes: grounding-unavailable stays a tool-side error that asks no daemon; diff-unavailable becomes a daemon error frame (or stays tool-side if the tool still assembles the diff). Add both cases to T17.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The caller and writer lists are complete: approveArtifactByJsonPath has two callers, reviewArtifactFile has two existing callers, finalizeArtifact has three, and the BUILD record has two build-step writers plus the approval-time writer.","evidence":"A search of non-test sources for each call found exactly: approveArtifactByJsonPath at src/workflow/gates.ts:759 and src/cli/services/workflow.ts:158; reviewArtifactFile at src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:346 and src/cli/services/workflow.ts:248; finalizeArtifact at src/mcp/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:46 and src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:260 and :283; persistBuildRecord at src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts:257 and src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts:85, plus persistStandaloneBuildRecord at src/mcp/build-step/phases/implement.ts:155. The daemon workflow.approve handler (src/daemon/index.ts:651) goes through approveWorkflowTarget. No daemon path writes code: runEditSession is called only at src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts:155 (the verdict session), so there is no daemon-authored build writer to stamp. The declared line numbers (gates.ts:562, 713, 759; orchestrator.ts:383; standalone-record.ts:270, 346; run-artifact.ts:68; runner.ts:158) all match. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/mcp/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/implement.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"None. Note for the plan: authoredBy has to reach the meta built inside each per-workflow finalizer in orchestrator.ts (about ten sites that set `attribution: attribution ?? singleModelAttribution(model)`), not just the finalizeArtifact signature.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon code-review request can take a `degraded` mode and then ground on the diff, stamp the record degraded and cap the verdict at warn, by changing src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts and passing the existing runner options through.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts:94-102 already has groundingMode and capVerdictAtWarn; line 192 folds with the cap, line 276 stamps `groundingMode: opts.groundingMode ?? 'full'`, and lines 307-311 reject a degraded record with a bare pass. But the options only stamp and cap: the grounding itself comes from `deps.assembleGrounding` (runner.ts:172), and the controller path gets diff grounding by injecting deps and re-keying `subject.changedFiles` to the diff-derived set (handler.ts:349-364, 463-471). The daemon handler passes no deps today (code-review-rpc.ts:93-99). The listed change site is therefore sufficient, provided the daemon does both extra steps. [files: src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts, src/mcp/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"State in 3.3 that the daemon's degraded mode must inject diff grounding through the runner's deps (same base and ledger exclusions as handler.ts:349-352) and re-key the subject's changedFiles; passing groundingMode alone would stamp `degraded` over graph grounding.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A BUILD record keeps an authoredBy it already carries when a later write (the approval-time writer) omits it, and the gate's existing block-and-override behaviour is unchanged by the additions.","evidence":"src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts:350-358 builds the merged meta as `...prior.meta, ...rec.meta`, so a field the new write omits survives; completion-record.ts:58-63 writes only workflow, epicHash, storyId, createdAt, updatedAt and standalone. The existing gate (gates.ts:575-591) throws ReviewBlockedError on a blocking verdict without an override, and approveWorkflowTarget catches it into skipped[] (gates.ts:758-766), which is the path the design reuses. One detail: today `reviewOverride` is recorded only inside the blocking-verdict branch (gates.ts:578-590), so an override given for an artifact with no review records nothing. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"In the build, record `reviewOverride` for the new causes too (no review, same-party review), since the current code would not; add that assertion to T5/T7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older records stay readable: a controller-authored artifact written before this change is identifiable by the stored label 'client' in meta.attribution.outputs, and a controller review by meta.review.model 'client'.","evidence":"src/mcp/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:46-52 calls finalizeArtifact with no model, so it defaults to 'client' (orchestrator.ts:394); each finalizer writes `attribution: attribution ?? singleModelAttribution(model)` (orchestrator.ts:451, 693, 866, ...), and attribution.ts:34-41, 50-52 keeps the raw label in `model`, giving one output with model 'client'. The daemon run passes a real per-step attribution (workflow-rpc.ts:260), never 'client'. ReviewReport.model is a required string (src/workflow/review/types.ts:156) and the controller phases stamp 'client' (findings.ts:71, verdicts.ts:73). The field references in the design are slightly off: OutputModelStamp.model is at types.ts:286 as cited, but ReviewReport.model is at review/types.ts:156, not :142. [files: src/workflow/attribution.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/mcp/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts, src/workflow/review/types.ts]","action":"Correct the citation to src/workflow/review/types.ts:156. No design change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion has a test that fails without the fix, the fake-daemon seam the integration tests need exists, and the existing suites the design says will break really do.","evidence":"Seam: src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts:66-68 `RunWorkflowStreamDeps.connect` and :197-199 `UnaryRpcDeps.connect` inject the socket factory. The four review-tool suites named in 3.5 exist, and review-step-findings.test.ts has no authoredBy, attribution or model on its fixtures, so they would route to the daemon as the design says. A search for the two approve functions finds 31 test files, matching the design's count. Mapping: ac1 to T9/T10/T12/T14-T17, ac2 to T1-T4, ac3 to T5-T8/T18, ac4 to T11, ac5 to T13; each asserts behaviour absent today (no party fields, no routing, gates.ts:578 approves an unreviewed DEF). Gaps, neither leaving a criterion unproven: no test covers the grounding-unavailable and diff-unavailable exits, and none asserts the override reason is recorded for the new no-review cause. [files: src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts, src/mcp/review-step/__tests__/review-step-findings.test.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"Extend T17 with the two error exits and T5/T7 with an assertion that `reviewOverride` is written when an unreviewed artifact is approved with a reason.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-05T08:46:29.047Z","model":"cli-claude:opus"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
